        "worked_solution": "Let's construct our matrix:\n\n- The index $3$ in ${J}_{3}(-2)$ means that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- The value $-2$ in ${J}_{3}(-2)$ means that we have $-2$'s on the main diagonal.\n\n- Also, we must have $1$'s on the superdiagonal (the diagonal above the main one).\n\nGiven that all the other entries must be zero, our Jordan block is\n\n$$\n{J}_{3}(-2)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
